      "answerEn": "Use he, has, ha, hemos, habéis, or han followed by the verb’s completed-action form.",
      "noteEn": "These are forms of haber, the helper verb used here like English “have.” For most verbs, the completed-action form ends in -ado after an -ar verb and -ido after an -er or -ir verb. This form is called the past participle, and it does not change after haber. How often this tense is used instead of the simple past varies by region.",
